cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this template repository in your research, please cite it using
  the metadata below.

title: >
  Synthea-OMOP Study Development Template: An End-to-End Observational Study Pipeline for OMOP CDM
  using OHDSI HADES and Synthea Synthetic Data

authors:
  - name: "OMOP Study Template Contributors"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-04-27"

repository-code: "https://github.com/adam-mdmph/synthea-omop-dev"
url: "https://github.com/adam-mdmph/synthea-omop-dev"

license: GPL-3.0

abstract: >
  A GitHub Template Repository providing an end-to-end pipeline for observational
  studies on an OMOP CDM v5.4 SQL Server database. Supports cohort characterization,
  prognostic modelling, and causal inference using the OHDSI HADES R toolstack.
  Includes synthetic data generation via Synthea for reproducible development and
  testing. Workflow steps cover environment setup, cohort definition, ETL to OMOP,
  data quality assessment (ACHILLES, Data Quality Dashboard), analysis, and
  manuscript-format report generation.

keywords:
  - OMOP CDM
  - OHDSI
  - observational study
  - real-world data
  - clinical informatics
  - PatientLevelPrediction
  - CohortMethod
  - FeatureExtraction
  - Synthea
  - R

